WEBVTT


00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.880
What's a perfectly productive

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:03.580
day in the life of Jeff Bezos?

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.040
I get up in the morning and I Potter.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.240
I like, I like have a coffee.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:11.000
I slowly move around.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.520
I'm not as productive as you might think I am

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.360
cause I do believe in wandering

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.200
and I read my phone for a while.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.600
I read newspapers for a while.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.060
I chat with Laura and I drink my first coffee.

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.680
So I kind of,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.840
I move pretty slowly in the first couple of hours.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.820
I get up early

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.140
just naturally.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:32.520
I exercise most days

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.760
and most days it's not that hard for me.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.140
Some days it's really hard

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.000
and I do it anyway.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.360
I don't want to, you know,

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:39.840
and it's painful and I'm like,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:40.800
why am I here?

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.680
And I don't want to do,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.800
why am I here at the gym?

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:44.960
Why am I here at the gym?

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.480
Why don't I do something else?

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.180
It's not always easy.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.900
What's your source of motivation in those moments?

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:54.720
I know that I'll feel better later if I do it.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.720
And so like the real source of motivation,

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.940
I can tell the days when I skip it.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.840
I'm not, I'm not quite as alert.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.320
I don't feel as good.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.380
I do a little bit of cardio

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:08.040
and a little bit of weightlifting and

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:08.920
um, I rotate.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.360
I do a pulling day and a pushing day and a leg day.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:13.040
It's all pretty standard stuff.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.460
So puttering, coffee,

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:15.880
buttering, coffee,

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:16.906
gym and Then work.
